    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0284" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 294/176: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-04-11T14:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 11,
                                1923—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:03 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>190. W–26. … The Department is correct in its assumption that current European
                    army costs have priority in each year under the proposed paragraph 8, section
                        2.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d95-f1"/> From the beginning it has been the
                    position of the Allies that before the United States priority should be applied
                    their current army costs must be met. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>[Wadsworth]</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d95-f1" n="7" xml:id="d95-f1-content">
                <p>Art. 2, par. <hi rendition="#small-caps">viii</hi>, of agreement signed on May
                    25, <ref target="#pg180">p. 180</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
